  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "22257d5f-6d71-4a62-afce-8a188309e2f0",
      "name": "📌 Overview – How This Workflow Works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -928,
        -112
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 724,
        "content": "## 📒 Create Product in Pricebooks – GHL Custom Object Sync\n\n### How it works\nThis workflow creates product and price book entry records in GoHighLevel custom objects, driven by a Google Sheets product list. A webhook trigger fires when a new product is ready to sync. The workflow reads the product rows from Sheets, filters to those without a `Creation Status`, and creates a `custom_objects.products` record in GHL for each one. After updating the row status, it reads the `Pricebook` column — which supports comma-separated pricebook names. Each name is split into its own loop item. For every pricebook, GHL is searched by name, a `price_book_entry` custom object record is created, and two GHL associations are made: product → pricebook, and price book entry → product.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Replace `YOUR_GHL_API_TOKEN` in the Authorization header of all HTTP Request nodes.\n2. Replace `YOUR_GHL_LOCATION_ID` in all request bodies.\n3. Replace `YOUR_GHL_PRODUCT_PRICEBOOK_ASSOCIATION_ID` in the Associate Product to Named Pricebook node.\n4. Replace `YOUR_GHL_PBE_PRODUCT_ASSOCIATION_ID` in the Associate PBE to Product node.\n5. Connect **Google Sheets OAuth2** to the Sheets nodes — replace `YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID`.\n6. Confirm sheet columns match: `Product Name`, `Brand`, `Pricebook` (comma-separated), `Creation Status`.\n7. Set the Webhook production URL as the trigger in your source system."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "185dab41-e714-4df9-b4f1-65541ece6320",
      "name": "Section – Sheet Read, Filter & Product Creation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -128,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1188,
        "height": 552,
        "content": "## 📋 Sheet Read, Filter & Product Creation\nWebhook triggers the read of all product rows from Google Sheets. Rows with an existing `Creation Status` are filtered out. For each new row, a `custom_objects.products` record is created in GHL, then the sheet row is marked as processed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e8c7a52d-32cc-4688-8851-dac299bb26d3",
      "name": "Section – Pricebook Loop, PBE Creation & Association",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1072,
        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1592,
        "height": 808,
        "content": "## 🔄 Pricebook Loop, PBE Creation & Association\nSplits the comma-separated `Pricebook` column into individual loop items. For each pricebook: searches GHL by name, creates a `price_book_entry` custom object, then creates two associations — product → pricebook and PBE → product — before looping to the next pricebook."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "24d1e4c5-0622-45b5-89fd-f4f4c75f0038",
      "name": "🔑 Credentials & Configuration",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2688,
        400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 414,
        "content": "## 🔑 Credentials & GHL IDs\n- **GHL Private Integration Token** → `YOUR_GHL_API_TOKEN`\n- Replace `YOUR_GHL_LOCATION_ID` in all request bodies\n- Replace both association IDs in the two association nodes\n- **Google Sheets OAuth2** → `YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID`\n\nNever hardcode real tokens or IDs in shared templates."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
